"""The claims the 1871 story jaunts stand on (build.py). Each is a jaunt evidence record:
text, confidence, sources, locator (attested) or reasoning (inferred), liberty (reconstructed).

Quotations inside a claim's text are copied from the source as read: the Internet Archive's
plain-text OCR of Andreas vol. II (historyofchicago02andr), Sheahan and Upton (cu31924028806855)
and Colbert and Chamberlin (cu31924028806814), corrected only where the machine misread a
letter; the museum's pages and the NWS page as their live text reads. A stop that quotes
must cite the claim holding the quotation (tools/audit_jaunt_refusals.py).
"""

